===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|Amaryllis}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˌæməˈɹɪlɪs/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# The {{vern|belladonna lily}}, {{taxlink|Amaryllis belladonna|species|noshow=1|ver=161029}}, native to South Africa.
# A similar lily in genus {{taxlink|Hippeastrum|genus|noshow=1|ver=161029}}, such as {{taxlink|Hippeastrum puniceum|species|noshow=1|ver=161029}}, and cultivars.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|Amaryllis belladona}} {{l|en|belladonna lily}}, {{l|en|naked-lady-lily}}, {{vern|Jersey lily}}, {{l|en|amarillo}}, {{vern|March lily}} {{qualifier|South Africa}}

====Usage notes====
The plural {{m|en|amaryllides}} also exists, but is obsolete.

